{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-119512",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{1}{3}$ as $\\frac{5}{15}$ and $\\frac{3}{5}$ as $\\frac{9}{15},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{15}-\\frac{9}{15}=\\frac{5-9}{15}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $5-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/96aeff6f68fcb31f7a871381a819951ee749114228535155b2eda3b32aee8fef.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{5-9}{15}=\\frac{-4}{15}=-\\frac{4}{15}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
